Subject: [PATCH] linker: use dependency-first order for dynamic ELF executables

GHC collects packages in dependent-first order. Emit Haskell packages
dependency-first for dynamic ELF executables to reduce startup symbol lookup
costs.

Warm-cache launches on x86_64 Linux (Ryzen AI 9 365, GHC 9.6.6), using
pandoc 3.11 and git-annex 10.20260901. Copies of the installed executables
differ only in Haskell DT_NEEDED order; code and libraries are unchanged.

Mean +/- standard deviation over 100 runs per variant, in two 50-run
batches with reversed command order and 10 warmups per batch:

  Command             Dependent-first     Dependency-first    Reduction
  pandoc --version    173.1 +/- 12.0 ms     90.2 +/- 7.1 ms      47.9%
  git-annex version   178.1 +/-  8.7 ms     85.2 +/- 9.4 ms      52.2%

--- a/compiler/GHC/Linker/Unit.hs
+++ b/compiler/GHC/Linker/Unit.hs
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 where
 
 import GHC.Prelude
+import GHC.Platform
 import GHC.Platform.Ways
 import GHC.Unit.Types
 import GHC.Unit.Info
@@ -29,7 +30,14 @@
 getUnitLinkOpts :: GhcNameVersion -> Ways -> UnitEnv -> [UnitId] -> IO ([String], [String], [String])
 getUnitLinkOpts namever ways unit_env pkgs = do
     ps <- mayThrowUnitErr $ preloadUnitsInfo' unit_env pkgs
-    return (collectLinkOpts namever ways ps)
+    let hs_pkgs
+          | hasWay ways WayDyn
+          , osElfTarget (platformOS (ue_platform unit_env))
+          = reverse ps
+          | otherwise = ps
+        hs_libs = concatMap (map ("-l" ++) . unitHsLibs namever ways) hs_pkgs
+        (_, extra_libs, other_flags) = collectLinkOpts namever ways ps
+    return (hs_libs, extra_libs, other_flags)
 
 collectLinkOpts :: GhcNameVersion -> Ways -> [UnitInfo] -> ([String], [String], [String])
 collectLinkOpts namever ways ps =
